.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH conduct 1  "conduct 0.0.0-dev"
.SH NAME
conduct \- Conduct a typed node arrangement.
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBconduct\fR [\fB\-\-check\fR] [\fB\-\-explain\fR] [\fB\-\-run\fR] [\fB\-\-format\fR] [\fB\-\-diagnostic\-format\fR] [\fB\-\-color\fR] [\fB\-q\fR|\fB\-\-quiet\fR] [\fB\-v \fR]... [\fB\-\-verbose\-diagnostics\fR] [\fB\-\-compile\-input\fR] [\fB\-\-compatibility\-demo\fR] [\fB\-\-enable\-file\-write\fR] [\fB\-\-enable\-file\-watch\fR] [\fB\-\-enable\-storage\-cache\fR] [\fB\-\-enable\-process\-exec\fR] [\fB\-\-enable\-socket\-loopback\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] [\fIPANEL\fR] [\fIsubcommands\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Conduct a typed node arrangement.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-check\fR
Parse, resolve, and validate without starting nodes
.TP
\fB\-\-explain\fR
Show exact node, port, cord, type, and flow resolution
.TP
\fB\-\-run\fR
Run the panel (the default mode)
.TP
\fB\-\-format\fR \fI<FORMAT>\fR [default: human]
Select human, finite JSON, or streaming NDJSON primary output
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
human
.IP \(bu 2
json
.IP \(bu 2
ndjson
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-diagnostic\-format\fR \fI<DIAGNOSTIC_FORMAT>\fR [default: human]
Select human or lossless JSON diagnostics on stderr
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
human
.IP \(bu 2
json
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-color\fR \fI<COLOR>\fR [default: auto]
Select diagnostic terminal styling
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
auto
.IP \(bu 2
always
.IP \(bu 2
never
.RE
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Suppress nonessential status and progress, never values or diagnostics
.TP
\fB\-v\fR
Add bounded resolution status detail; repeat for future detail levels
.TP
\fB\-\-verbose\-diagnostics\fR
Include related spans, notes, paths, and causes
.TP
\fB\-\-compile\-input\fR \fI<INPUT>\fR
Resolve and run against this explicit compile\-input snapshot
.TP
\fB\-\-compatibility\-demo\fR
Run the finite batch compatibility demo instead of an exact plan
.TP
\fB\-\-enable\-file\-write\fR
Explicitly install the bounded example file\-write provider
.TP
\fB\-\-enable\-file\-watch\fR
Explicitly install the bounded example file\-watch provider
.TP
\fB\-\-enable\-storage\-cache\fR
Explicitly install the bounded evictable blob\-cache provider
.TP
\fB\-\-enable\-process\-exec\fR
Explicitly install the bounded closed\-inventory process provider
.TP
\fB\-\-enable\-socket\-loopback\fR
Explicitly install the bounded numeric\-loopback socket providers
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.TP
[\fIPANEL\fR]
Read editable source from this file, or `\-`/no path for stdin
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
conduct\-inspect(1)
Validate and describe one artifact without executing it
.TP
conduct\-compile(1)
Compile source against explicit immutable inputs into one exact plan
.TP
conduct\-package(1)
Create, verify, or extract a bounded content\-addressed package
.SH VERSION
v0.0.0\-dev
.SH STREAMS
Primary human values, finite JSON results, and streaming NDJSON run records are written to stdout.
Diagnostics and terminal status are written to stderr.
.SH MACHINE OUTPUT
\fB\-\-format=json\fR selects a finite conduit.result record for check or explain.
\fB\-\-format=ndjson\fR selects ordered, bounded conduit.run channel chunks and structured records for run.
\fB\-\-diagnostic\-format=json\fR independently selects one structured diagnostic on stderr.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Zero indicates success, help, version, or normal downstream pipe closure.
Two indicates a command, source, resolution, runtime, or non-broken output failure.
